  "title": "Stochastic differential equations",
  "html": "<h1>Stochastic differential equations</h1><p>Brownian increments in an SDE scale as √Δt. Adding random numbers to an ODE solver does not by itself specify the stochastic interpretation or convergence order.</p><h2 id=\"model\">Problem and representative equations</h2><p>The formula uses a scalar Itô SDE. a is drift, b is diffusion and ΔWₙ are independent Gaussian increments with mean zero and variance Δt. Euler–Maruyama evaluates both coefficients at n. Converting a Stratonovich equation requires the appropriate drift correction.</p><div class=\"math-block\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>d</mi><mi>W</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"/><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dX=a(X,t)\\,dt+b(X,t)\\,dW,\\qquad X_{n+1}=X_n+a(X_n,t_n)\\Delta t+b(X_n,t_n)\\Delta W_n.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">W</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0785em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2083em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0785em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0785em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">Δ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0785em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">Δ</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">W</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div><h2 id=\"algorithm\">Algorithm</h2><p>Generate Wiener increments and advance deterministic and stochastic terms. Strong-error refinement must couple paths by summing fine increments into the coarse increment. Weak error concerns expectations of test functions, not the discrepancy of one pair of paths.</p><h2 id=\"conditions\">Conditions and pitfalls</h2><p>Under suitable global Lipschitz, moment and smoothness assumptions, Euler–Maruyama typically has strong order 1/2 and weak order 1. Superlinear growth or positivity constraints can invalidate the method and require specialized treatments. Sampling uncertainty may dominate weak discretization error.</p><h2 id=\"verification\">What to check</h2><p>Use geometric Brownian exact paths and Ornstein–Uhlenbeck moments to test strong and weak convergence separately. Record step size, random streams, sample count and uncertainty, including negative states or boundary violations.</p><h2 id=\"publication-scope\">Publication scope and related entries</h2><p>Euler–Maruyama for scalar geometric Brownian motion. Coarse/fine steps and analytic endpoints share the same Brownian paths; measure strong RMS error across 4096 paths. Does not validate general SDEs, MCMC or weak convergence order. Inputs, code, measured values and tolerances are linked from the method and execution pages. Not every general verification proposal above has been executed.</p><ul><li><a href=\"/numerical-methods-atlas/methods/sde/?lang=en\">Stochastic differential equations</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sources\">Primary publications, supporting sources and review scope</h2><p>Distinguish original research, later variants, author monographs, pedagogical articles and official references. Bibliographic verification differs from consulting selected passages; neither implies a full-paper audit or numerical reproduction. Access-depth notes accompany each source.</p><ol class=\"reading-sources\"><li id=\"source-maruyama1955\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/bf02846028\">Gisiro Maruyama (1955). Continuous Markov processes and stochastic equations</a>. Rendiconti del Circolo Matematico di Palermo<p>Research publication: proposal or related formulation · Bibliography checked · <a href=\"https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1007%2FBF02846028\">Consulted record</a></p><p>Bibliographic identity checked against the DOI registration on 2026-11-22. Relevant abstracts or selected passages are separately identified in the detailed-reading source notes; this is not a claim of a full-paper audit or numerical reproduction.</p></li><li id=\"source-higham2001\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1137/s0036144500378302\">Desmond J. Higham (2001). An Algorithmic Introduction to Numerical Simulation of Stochastic Differential Equations</a>. SIAM Review<p>Pedagogical account, distinct from the original proposal · Selected source passages consulted · <a href=\"https://epubs.siam.org/doi/pdf/10.1137/S0036144500378302\">Consulted record</a></p><p>Introductory methods and convergence distinctions; this is pedagogical supporting literature, not the original Euler–Maruyama proposal.</p></li></ol>",
